3. Access key
StarX asks for a key that is shared in the StarX Discord server. The key is
only a way to join the community. Do not post it publicly. Access may be
withdrawn for anyone who breaks the server rules or these terms.

4. System changes and your responsibility
StarX changes settings on your PC: display color and resolution, the active
power plan, current-user and system registry values, per-game compatibility
flags, audio volume and game configuration files. StarX records the original
values and restores them when you turn a feature off or exit. If StarX is
killed, crashes, or loses power, a restore can be interrupted; run
"StarX.exe --reset" to put display state back, or turn the feature off in the
app.

Some tweaks write to the system part of the registry and need administrator
rights; StarX skips them when it does not have that access.

5. Games and anti-cheat
StarX does not inject code into games, read or write game memory, or hook game
processes. It edits settings and configuration files on disk and changes
Windows display state. Game publishers and anti-cheat services set their own
rules, and StarX cannot promise how any game or service will treat a
particular setting. You use StarX in online games at your own risk, and StarX
is not responsible for bans, suspensions or lost progress.

